<article class="env-lemma" id="00T3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00T3">Lemma <span data-tag="00T3">10.137.2</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a smooth ring map. Any localization $S_ g$ is smooth over $R$. If $f \in R$ maps to an invertible element of $S$, then $R_ f \to S$ is smooth. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/00S7" data-tag="00S7">10.134.13</a> the naive cotangent complex for $S_ g$ over $R$ is the base change of the naive cotangent complex of $S$ over $R$. The assumption is that the naive cotangent complex of $S/R$ is $\Omega _{S/R}$ and that this is a finite projective $S$-module. Hence so is its base change. Thus $S_ g$ is smooth over $R$. 
    <p>
      The second assertion follows in the same way from Lemma <a href="/tag/07BS" data-tag="07BS">10.134.11</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>